@startuml Decorator-Middleware-Sequence
title How a request travels through the chain (one failure, then success, then a cache hit)

actor Client
participant "aTimingPriceFeed" as T
participant "aLoggingPriceFeed" as L
participant "aCachingPriceFeed" as C
participant "aRetryingPriceFeed" as R
participant "theSupplier" as S

== request 1 — cache miss, one failure, retried ==

Client -> T : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate T
T -> T : startedAt = clock.now()
T -> L : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate L
L -> L : log "asking for SKU-200"
L -> C : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate C
C -> C : miss
C -> R : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate R
R -> S : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate S
S --> R : FeedUnavailableException
deactivate S
R -> R : retryable, attempt 2
R -> S : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate S
S --> R : Quote(249.00)
deactivate S
R --> C : Quote(249.00)
deactivate R
C -> C : store, stamped with clock.now()
C --> L : Quote(249.00)
deactivate C
L -> L : log "got SKU-200 = 249.00 EUR"
L --> T : Quote(249.00)
deactivate L
T -> T : metrics.record(200 ms)
T --> Client : Quote(249.00)
deactivate T

== request 2 — cache hit; everything below the cache is skipped ==

Client -> T : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate T
T -> L : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate L
L -> L : log "asking for SKU-200"
L -> C : quoteFor("SKU-200")
activate C
C -> C : hit — **does not forward**
C --> L : Quote(249.00)
deactivate C
L -> L : log "got SKU-200 = 249.00 EUR"
L --> T : Quote(249.00)
deactivate L
T -> T : metrics.record(0 ms)
T --> Client : Quote(249.00)
deactivate T

note over C, S
  On the hit, the retry decorator and the supplier are never
  reached. That is why a rate limiter placed OUTSIDE the cache
  charges quota for calls that never happen, and one placed
  INSIDE charges only for real traffic.
end note

note over Client, S
  The client called one method on one object and got a Quote.
  It cannot tell that five objects were involved — that is the
  transparency the pattern buys, and also the reason a stack
  trace from here is five frames deeper than you expect.
end note

@enduml
